# Repaired 2026-08-24. The first line of this file was written with LITERAL
# backslash-n sequences instead of newlines, so git read eight rules as one
# comment and ignored NOTHING -- not .env, not node_modules, not dist. Verified
# with `git check-ignore -q .env` returning not-ignored in a repo whose
# .env.example names a GitHub dispatch token. Same defect fused NUL to the
# filename below it. Nothing had leaked: no .env exists on disk and only
# .env.example is tracked.

# Dependencies
node_modules/
# Builds
dist/
build/
# Env
.env
.env.*
# OS/editor
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
.vscode/

# Windows reserved device name
NUL
deployment-prep-report.json
__pycache__/
*.pyc
public/data/version.json
scripts/game-integration-config.json

# Claude Code machine-local settings (permissions granted on this machine).
# The .local suffix means per-machine by convention; tracking it makes every
# permission grant a merge conflict.
.claude/settings.local.json
content_audit.json
page_audit.json

# Internal review builds. These live INSIDE the deploy root (public/), so they are
# one `git add -A` away from being published to pdoom1.com -- and two workflows
# (weekly-league-reset.yml, weekly-deployment.yml) stage the whole tree that way.
# Untracked is not enough on its own; ignored is.
public/_review/

# Agent worktrees. Claude Code creates these under .claude/worktrees/ and a
# stray `git add -A` sweeps the whole embedded checkout into a commit -- that
# happened twice on 2026-08-24, once burying another agent's uncommitted edits
# inside a PR whose body described two changes and whose commit made four.
# .git-worktrees/ is listed too because CLAUDE.md and an earlier handover both
# named it; it is not the path in use, and ignoring a path that does not exist
# costs nothing while ignoring the wrong one cost a session.
.claude/worktrees/
.git-worktrees/
